  "details": "As a world creator i often close the instance of the world i was testing and reload.\n\nBecause of this workflow I accidently cleared my local user data for the Fish! world. Please add a way to restore persistent data when this happens. I did it so quick i didn't even see the warning prompt. The UI should not be designed in this way especially since players can also pay real money for items in the world. \n\nAs you can see in the pictures the buttons are in the same position. \n\nWhen you are not the owner of an instance the 6th button is \"Reset user data\" but when you do own the instance the 6th button is \"Close instance\". \n\nPlease, \n\nAdd a setting to outright disable the button from showing.\n\nAdd like a type to confirm prompt, not a click confirm.\n\nMake the user type \"Confirm\"\n\nOr add a setting to restore persistent data within 7 days.\n\nRIP like 50 hours of my life.",
